# Web UI Standards (`apps/web`)

## Design tokens

Use semantic Tailwind tokens from `tailwind.config.ts`. Do not introduce one-off hex colors.

| Token                                        | Use for                         |
| -------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------- |
| `surface`, `surface-muted`                   | Page/card backgrounds           |
| `content`, `content-muted`, `content-subtle` | Text hierarchy                  |
| `line`                                       | Dividers, card borders          |
| `accent`, `accent-foreground`                | Primary actions, active filters |
| `danger-*`                                   | Error states                    |

Layout utilities:

- `page-container` — max width + horizontal padding (use on every page section)
- `max-w-page` — 72rem content width

## Component rules

1. **Reuse `components/ui/*`** before creating new primitives (`Button`, `Panel`, `Pill`, `SectionHeader`, `EmptyState`, `Alert`, `Skeleton`, `Pagination`, `PageShell`).
2. **Page layout** — wrap pages in `PageShell` (header + footer). Content goes in `page-container`.
3. **Sections** — use `SectionHeader` for page titles; wrap filters/toolbars in `Panel`.
4. **Spacing** — page sections use `space-y-8`; grids use `gap-6`.
5. **Radius** — cards/panels: `rounded-2xl`; buttons: `rounded-lg`; pills: `rounded-full`.
6. **Shadows** — cards: `shadow-card`; panels/dropdowns: `shadow-panel`. Avoid custom shadow values.

## Category filters

- Show **All + top 5 categories** as `Pill` components.
- Put overflow categories in a **More** dropdown (never render 10+ pills inline).
- Single-select only — no separate “clear filter” control.

## Data fetching

- Use TanStack Query in client page components.
- API calls live in `lib/api.ts`; formatting helpers in `lib/format.ts`.
- Shared response types come from `@repo/shared`.

## Adding a new page

```tsx
// app/example/page.tsx
import { PageShell } from '@/components/ui/page-shell';
import { SectionHeader } from '@/components/ui/section-header';

export default function ExamplePage() {
  return (
    <PageShell>
      <div className="page-container space-y-8">
        <SectionHeader title="Title" description="Description" />
        {/* content */}
      </div>
    </PageShell>
  );
}
```

## Do not

- Use raw `gray-*` / `slate-*` for new UI — use semantic tokens.
- Duplicate button/pill/card styles inline — extend `components/ui/*`.
- Add sidebar category lists — use horizontal pills + More dropdown.
- Put business logic in `components/ui/*` — keep UI primitives presentational.
